      'How would you test a pen?',
      'Ask clarifying questions first, then think of functional, non functional and destructive tests.',
      'Start by asking about requirements: type of pen, users, ink colour, expected lifetime. Then test functionality (writes smoothly, ink colour, cap and click work), usability (grip, weight, easy to refill), performance (how many metres it writes, behaviour in cold or hot conditions), reliability (leaks, drops), compatibility (different papers) and safety (non toxic ink, cap with an air hole).',
      '<p>The interviewer is testing how you think, not your knowledge of pens. Asking about requirements first is the strongest signal you can give.</p>',
